ng with the Guhyakas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.828,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042022","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"beae77cf71565482c9d92fb6105775edfa4b474a95cc9eb1ac41842fbae9c09f","compact":"9d2e777442ec53d0f77b17c1300906e5078b2ce3c0964b42e01173e347ff5cb6","nasal":"9d2e777442ec53d0f77b17c1300906e5078b2ce3c0964b42e01173e347ff5cb6"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-23","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":23,"english":"In the offshoots belonging to Kailasa resembling the moon, as also in their caverns, do you thoroughly search for Rāvaņa in company with Vaidehī.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042023","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"895f4811eeddaf7200507caf53674a5a6f7bdaee85c9725a080b45fcd8dde82f","compact":"af354dc9ac48d98206ec6a8d4c87906e3abc6eb83c4fac22a044d300f47e0dd5","nasal":"06e855086e8b930fc7b84745773bb41a273ffdf452b43f0aa7e9027ecbcf4851"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-24","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":24,"english":"And coming to the Kruncha mountain, you should, having your wits about you, enter its inaccessible cavern; for that is well known as difficult of entrance.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042024","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2e7332f79e88c2ac49c1799abf38eb39fbcb376e535f2aeb6719a52bc683a93b","compact":"22d7f0926de74161713f357fc1234b70ee58ce26afad496e2fcc64b58d92323a","nasal":"741423bc4d030fed2a794ac12b1fbe47f5d0af1b2ffe13e068251890dfc4ebd6"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-25","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":25,"english":"There dwell certain Maharsis, high-souled, of effulgence resembling that of the sun-complete god-like shapes,—who are sought by the deities themselves.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.794,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042025","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"004a0102f73589e1f5d40d4e3a029ef2c89fe12b30d74cecac692e154abd2ab6","compact":"6b617ffee4b816457d2af582eae2dfd7a2d90751422e19a39f5b697404833645","nasal":"a9358b5f6bef6b1bb1f32f8f513867fa9c77e809fbe0449ac197e1eba3a8be21"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-26","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":26,"english":"And you should thoroughly explore the other caves of Krauncha, its plateaus and peaks; its passes and sides.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042026","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ff3ff90e611ba1d90f16b98a07c899b3e67e17333b5f9780f0124e7dc91bc360","compact":"41939ac94fa2c2060b15d60b78bcb0376ba742271055e1a0c45a34bf31edf517","nasal":"fad044f16b5fe3ff400b73a7dcdc7ec1c6690ca3a1789a0c63615540c790298a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-27","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":27,"english":"(Then is) the treeless Manasa-abode of birds-the scene of Kāma's austerities. Way there is none for creatures, or for gods, or for Raksasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.379,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042027","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ea4e91adeb9aa2a11bf900324176bdf9bb237d182240929b941ebfb6d90a6cda","compact":"0c320a309ae9f7d68396bc85222922fd048a99607e5dcae50b67643bf551718b","nasal":"8adf08037b7c5d0e4478c420dcc15e1f7418163f3afd9f5574dead76b98e762f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-28","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":28,"english":"are That also must be explored by you, that mountain with plains and plateous. Going beyond Krauncha, (you shall see) the mountain, named Maināka.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.458,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042028","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9087f5d2ecf2d9e21b925fe51b6c5870aa4c9c1a140482f61c357b48017fd4a9","compact":"dab40c181ae5127c47ef248f04339a7e9607d0f9d2fde2ab09c870dd728cc8e9","nasal":"dab40c181ae5127c47ef248f04339a7e9607d0f9d2fde2ab09c870dd728cc8e9"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-29","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":29,"english":"are That also must be explored by you, that mountain with plains and plateous. Going beyond Krauncha, (you shall see) the mountain, named Maināka. There is the residence of the Danvava, Maya, reared by himself. Mainaka also with its plains, plateaus and woods must be searched by you.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.492,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-25","DUTT-4-43-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042029","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"32c38fdea7805215cb1a1255327daeb3fec29e16bd335a38aa5c058800988f60","compact":"fd77e93eb73fa7e239403406ab205241789a091ce2b02153318b1231dff6c297","nasal":"9941f6175a8faa106d3ea449a58ecfebb8af7d02d929bba962d98bd1d28c2ab1"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-30","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":30,"english":"There is the residence of the Danvava, Maya, reared by himself. Mainaka also with its plains, plateaus and woods must be searched by you. There are all over, the homes of females with faces resembling those of horses. Going beyond that part, (you shall come to) the asylum inhabited by Siddhas; where ascetics—Vālakhilyas, Siddhas and Vaikhānasas. Saluting those Siddhas, who have been cleansed of their sins on account of their asceticism, you should in humble guise ask them concerning Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.424,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-26","DUTT-4-43-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042030","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f82dec903f211478dfbde7f89706a3443f47b48ebc79f099256b5964827bb823","compact":"5d717c2f623c50969e170d467709c8566b424cb4eeef7573d5800f7c07a619c9","nasal":"6d2d1f8c22ebd1494553687d048927cb49f5699b3ea145366b1524bdb858ba6c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-31","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":31,"english":"There are all over, the homes of females with faces resembling those of horses. Going beyond that part, (you shall come to) the asylum inhabited by Siddhas; where ascetics—Vālakhilyas, Siddhas and Vaikhānasas. Saluting those Siddhas, who have been cleansed of their sins on account of their asceticism, you should in humble guise ask them concerning Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.781,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042031","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4238272971490251fccd5e1b257004b01aa87b07c626f282e865c79463775bc2","compact":"d801be418f3549d62d5bdc6584aebb90f77117d0a2a7f4b5ee8f0c4691af30ff","nasal":"d801be418f3549d62d5bdc6584aebb90f77117d0a2a7f4b5ee8f0c4691af30ff"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-32","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":32,"english":"There are all over, the homes of females with faces resembling those of horses. Going beyond that part, (you shall come to) the asylum inhabited by Siddhas; where ascetics—Vālakhilyas, Siddhas and Vaikhānasas. Saluting those Siddhas, who have been cleansed of their sins on account of their asceticism, you should in humble guise ask them concerning Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.474,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042032","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"be4127c13399fca1951f8a412cd8f1327e97295b61ac86c61c85d789ec71dc2d","compact":"75d14cd839f4d4599cb2dfbc427b7764339961fd4ee46b2d0f0ce1ae74cf22b5","nasal":"71a27e7ff0ae62dce3d249b4036000614e2e7513a57db5f2036e419bf1fa7bba"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-33","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":33,"english":"There is the Vaikhānasa tank filled with golden lotuses; and ranged by graceful cranes of the hue of the infant sun.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.814,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042033","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"19ac5229277548594b7274ea5d66d9fb669c5e3645544dc32d5fbd41096052b4","compact":"e275a739cc67cd1ac70f0334e3fdad24244517e39ce2d5503e7a2e0f23642869","nasal":"ec9c7d45e800cd104dc5158841c18fde76c38840d4f8fddfd3774d55cb1efc7d"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-34","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":34,"english":"Kuvera's vehicle, the elephant known (by the name of) Sārvabhauma, ever rangeth that country in company with she-elephants.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.815,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042034","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2167d32ef77e709446fb7a10b8c28745c13dd2438bab02b30a0bac0b9fd049bf","compact":"4df2e71e28a05575bfc922b8c2a9142949749da5e8f3be95520d88e8b082040a","nasal":"4df2e71e28a05575bfc922b8c2a9142949749da5e8f3be95520d88e8b082040a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-35","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":35,"english":"Going beyond that expanse of water, (you come upon) a sky void of stars, and where the sun and the moon have been put out; and that land is visible by the rays, as if of the sun, proceeding from (the persons of) self-luminous, god-like ones, who are reposing there, after achieving success in austerities.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042035","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5eb7ad259ff4be64b66b8fa10c019b2a4cd7f4af6e0145fb5602b01d10eee5ff","compact":"eabc58389eefcf9ee25c9671de858c33bd2015838bc557d3dd5b8639f25a6ed7","nasal":"e0464bd3fcbde5f48e863a12f4fbc96feb6acaf550d3d28c969aead96c8e6e12"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-36","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":36,"english":"Going beyond that expanse of water, (you come upon) a sky void of stars, and where the sun and the moon have been put out; and that land is visible by the rays, as if of the sun, proceeding from (the persons of) self-luminous, god-like ones, who are reposing there, after achieving success in austerities.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.795,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042036","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ece6d45dd086cc986e02214476a123fb7b3e56c1ee71e3c6f4954d7a8cf74b2c","compact":"f822d9fef6c35c1740d33abb501dec8d553b0af42db94dbd55249bbaff2d2e35","nasal":"574efe9f8f4742a1a75103a3ede946229857d881b1590a30c132e9dd384d244c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-37","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":37,"english":"Leaving behind that region, (you come to) a stream named Sailoda. On its both banks are bamboos named Kīcaka.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.825,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042037","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e2deb45ca2563bf26051789b712cf6dcaa3020f8708409f57e6eec18d0c8916e","compact":"ba6bfd62cf48843a7bc8516033a89e78eabc586a040f3fc09e9df51133f852a8","nasal":"ba6bfd62cf48843a7bc8516033a89e78eabc586a040f3fc09e9df51133f852a8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-38","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":38,"english":"These take the Siddhas to the other shore and bring them back again. There (are seen the northern Kurus, the abode of those that have acquired religious merit.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.94,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042038","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4131c6703e56a6391a15f5d1370afb384156527df7391ab2c2a5fd1c268af331","compact":"c2c9068e69182be1ef375141e4879ebf21771b7d1a6563cccaaeed419745a7bd","nasal":"2c75b7787f196f7d1a80b21f6b4cd8aab2561f398c2dbe4404bb0c6f29990fb6"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-39","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":39,"english":"And there are tanks there with their waters crowned with golden lotuses. There are rivers by thousands with copious blue lapis leaves.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042039","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c86126083a9bd5234b2ea9b032eb0dcd7f61abbdf08eb7f752030f591d328e56","compact":"47ab78ab072d231551e8c4b3f8847c40b49e7486522946892746d5abb2c5a09c","nasal":"d95eeecdd4d30cb491468e2d33385d1e6d7223ab219c191e496e97021ddfef56"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-40","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":40,"english":"And the pools here, resembling the tender sun, are embellished with assemblages of golden red lotuses.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.8,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042040","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7935fc82bad6b8af8bee9b3627d084bd74688bfbf35be610c567fec06506381f","compact":"ef80ba48d28691a0e8f9c3a95d9282e19a2bcc03460beea8ff80c09df29724d6","nasal":"f4b152e116320fffdf6412c8635fa74d572586d6c1c66f2d7cf16e2149989123"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-41","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":41,"english":"And that tract is every where filled with costly gems, and jewels, and woods of blue lotuses, having filaments splendid like gold; and with round pearls and costly jewels.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042041","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c9cf2ebcc694f5f589bfccf826bea9e3c920d6c491b5978324ceae30d0ee1752","compact":"a9b1435d8009fd6a4fa1fbd0bb44c0a1de410a86d1df98104d4fdf007c2084d0","nasal":"3312f2a937bc8e8ca719842474097f484d02c54709ce80f88145a7d3761286d5"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-42","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":42,"english":"And the rivers there have islets covered with gold; and are crowded with lovely hills of gold, bright as fire, furnished with all kinds of precious stones.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.866,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042042","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7538f0b26311045b28fd859d0356d876c888a49a42bff1058360602899a91d61","compact":"75df39d33d4d66625ad54fb96e12b1e47fa9678fdaa3d3a27ed60