. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"59f0ee53cb3f9a5b945a5664dd0e5423eedfb699e2ead50e51b58e9ebdfc1b72","compact":"1d1cb38f1c31c57633230b15ad11a61f301ccd04d31e17b779f21535acb7267b","nasal":"c8ff982d6609fc7798eeec2ac95312f8c33dcb8a3a2c8fcb5868358373a26534"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-55","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":55,"english":"Albeit without the sun, yet through the brightness of the Soma mountain, the land shines forth with all the loveliness and reality of one warmed by the sun.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-45"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042055","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e802b24c20a195f76eaa4f318bfc94076e7887e575aac2eefdae6327a1fbbcc9","compact":"9537723851953905bea007c40e8f78e43434f861faaccabc98503f37fc87a7bb","nasal":"9537723851953905bea007c40e8f78e43434f861faaccabc98503f37fc87a7bb"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-56","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":56,"english":"There that Soul of the Universe, the adorable Sambhu, fraught with the spirits of the eleven Rudras-that lord of the gods-Brahmā.dwelleth, surrounded by the Brahmarsis.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.889,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-46"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042056","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"70f17cf9fc8b4f4706fdf3e549cb2d2ed701449c55372233f3b0a95d19b02a4b","compact":"c5a3666e334326f81a60cad0f4ad17a115bf51d4a9de580b6c70d6fb80d14086","nasal":"66b7b88312af7c592397b853400dfe6cb74f635680969e95c37abfe1e368c223"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-57","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":57,"english":"You cannot proceed to the north of the Kurus; nor is there way in that region for any other creatures.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.842,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-47"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042057","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5dcfdfa5e7be1fc1c6c01fd308ac8e0b1ad5f8dcf4031f8763d2ae571ecd1b33","compact":"b469901a2cdabd094c88391bc9191b851a1cb13538422a4ac9818e054d563990","nasal":"e986eeb0f9a08bcca265eadf402668d9f93902389fa44aa899598777c6c93bfb"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-58","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":58,"english":"And that mountain is named Soma, incapable of being entered even by the gods, Sighting this you should speedily turn back.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.78,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-48"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042058","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2b2d7533ffaa28a01fc8a39de31b1b1cd2b28f5e340870285b0439061a904fb5","compact":"86274f3f3bc470220ef960a764b56549cc128d2ab413988e351f1bdd4f9edd99","nasal":"86274f3f3bc470220ef960a764b56549cc128d2ab413988e351f1bdd4f9edd99"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-59","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":59,"english":"You foremost of monkeys, the monkeys are able to proceed thus far. Beyond this, of what is sunless and boundless I know nothing.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-42-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042059","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b0cf1d9f16adad41f80f3fb4fab9df35aebd33e04357ac9a98e43ed65b3551d6","compact":"e7278697ee3b0eada3c12f0703a54b44d274f47ce856d7df15579a408225af4c","nasal":"06a7e3b8e87b8ba01f235e9ab705f95afbf80d54e4bb8beb242e179a053657e9"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-60","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":60,"english":"You should search all these which I have described (to you); and you should also turn your attention to others besides, which I have omitted to mention.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-50"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042060","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f3c6b4ec656ba5085ac4d35c897ee9d845f465f1211091b430d9e090866a7a99","compact":"3b4b3714cf0479f0de8a062150a55d10fc4448fc221ce29a5663eb68a4c529c3","nasal":"3b4b3714cf0479f0de8a062150a55d10fc4448fc221ce29a5663eb68a4c529c3"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-61","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":61,"english":"You that are comparable to the wind or fire, by accomplishing the work of beholding Videha's daughter, you will do what is held as exceedingly dear to Daśaratha's son as well as highly grateful to me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.929,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-51"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042061","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a86a6deeb47fd89acf9132d4857b1455263af413f2dcd92932ba57b536c788fc","compact":"bd1fad64bfaa1120941f2be86dab153ab01e9c28b871c2ee8231d603fb7364a4","nasal":"bd1fad64bfaa1120941f2be86dab153ab01e9c28b871c2ee8231d603fb7364a4"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-42-62","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":42,"verse":62,"english":"Then, having achieved success, do you, along with your friends, honoured by me, and crowned with every virtue, you monkeys, with your enemies slain, range the earth in company with your wives,-the support of all beings.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.747,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-43-52"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4042062","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6b8c736563d1f33211030dc7f8cd7e46935e40295b2f192ee3979cf40a4736bd","compact":"72c2f5434a0e4657c8dfa